  "body": "https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1459671 was filed against Firefox because it uses a same origin check. Per investigation from @bzbarsky it appears that other browsers use same origin-domain. This means that you can target a cross-origin `<iframe>`'s name if you are same origin-domain with it.\r\n\r\nIt seems better if this concept does not depend on `document.domain`.\r\n\r\n@whatwg/security interested in fixing this in your respective implementations?\r\n\r\nEither way, we should probably also add a test for this as I don't think it's covered.",
